# User Preferences — Kirby

## Experience Level
Kirby is a new vibe coder who is learning as they go. They may not know standard dev terminology, CLI commands, or project conventions yet.

## Guidance Style
- **Explain WHY**, not just what — every command or change should come with a brief reason.
- **Don't assume knowledge** of git, npm, terminal, or build tools. If a workflow requires these, walk through it.
- **Avoid jargon** without context. If you use a term like "port", "server", or "dependency", give a one-liner explanation the first time.
- **Proactively teach** patterns they'll reuse (e.g. "this is how you start the app — you'll do this every time").
- **Don't repeat yourself** — if something was already explained in a previous rule or skill, reference it instead.

## Workflow Preferences
- Prefers seeing the app in the browser to verify changes visually.
- Likes quick feedback loops: make a change → see it live.
- Appreciates when the AI remembers context from earlier in the conversation so they don't have to re-explain.
